Fillets: a rounding rolling on an edge whose ends are cut by the faces at
the ends past where its ball comes tangent to the face of that edge
(mitcad#343).

The case: a groove of radius 5 runs under a slot's end wall, whose face is
left a strip 0.86 high above the groove between two concave roundings of 9
of the slot's ceiling; the groove passes through a notch in the wall's 1 mm
thickness, and beside the notch the wall goes on down to the groove's
other side. The groove's rim on the strip is rounded with 10: the ball's
contact on the strip's plane lies above the strip, so the ball rolls on the
strip's top edges (the 9 roundings' end sections and the ceiling's edge),
and the strip is consumed. At each end of the rim the notch's wall is the
face at the end. The walk went on past the ends, its contact on the groove
running off across the groove's edge with the wall beside the notch onto
that wall's plane, and both corners failed ("Corner OnSame : no point on
arc", "OneCorner : bouchon non ecrit"). The bodies stored in the files keep
the rolling blend up to where its ball comes tangent to the 9 rounding,
run its surface on along its tangents and cut it there by the wall beside
the notch (from where the contact on the groove crosses the groove's edge
with it), by the notch's wall and by the 9 rounding's surface, which grow
up to the cut.

- ChFi3d_Builder::RolledEndCutByEndFace (new, tried at each end of a
  stripe after WalkedOnSameToEndFace in PerformSetOfSurf): for an end piece
  P rolling on an edge Er of a face B whose contact on the other side, on
  face N, ends on an edge A of N into a face Fa (any pieces past P walked
  on over Fa), at a spine's end vertex V of three faces (N, the face Fref
  across Er and the face at the end Be): the blend is walked again from
  P's middle with N's surface unbounded (ChFi3d_FaceWidened) rolling on Er
  up to its end, made again a little short of it where the approximation
  of its singular last section fails; its surface is run on along its
  tangents (GeomLib::ExtendSurfByLength, C1) and cut by Fa from the point
  A1 where the contact on N crosses A, by Be from the point on the line of
  Fa's edge with Be (that edge's vertex where the point lies on it), and
  by B from the point Q on the curve of B and Be up to the point T where
  that intersection ends on the contact on Er (ChFi3d_CutBetween,
  ChFi3d_CutToLineEnd: branches of the surfaces' intersection lines). The
  contact on Er ends at T. Be grows up to the cut along its edges with
  Fref and Fa prolonged (to Er's crossing E3 with Be, and to the cut's
  point) and its curve with B from E3 to Q, which B grows up to as well;
  Er is cut at E3 and at T, the edge of N and Be and the spine's edge at
  V are taken by the blend. The end is put in the data structure (the
  stripe's end points, InDS) with no corner; the pieces past P go, and the
  re-walked piece's face is generated by the spine's edges P's is.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformFilletOnVertex: no corner at the end of a lone
  stripe already in the data structure there.
- ChFi3d_ExtendAtSpineEnds: an arc that is no edge of the shape (of a face
  made of a surface unbounded) is not looked up in the edge/face map.

On the design's body before the item (two edges of the rim, both ends cut
this way): valid, every face of the result on the stored body's within
1.6e-4 mm both ways, the material within a box round the rounding
207.3352 against the stored body's 207.3360 mm3; before, both corners
failed. Synthetic: a block's slot rounded with 9 along its ceiling's long
edges, a groove of radius 5 under its end wall through a notch, the
groove's rim on the strip rounded with 10: valid, both notch walls grown up
to the cut above the groove's rim, the 9 roundings grown a little past the
slot's wall; before, both corners failed.

Upstream: new.
